    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T18:38:11Z",
    "body": "Port onto the current frame: head `fa31e7120`. This head merges the #2992 head `db8a61aba` into this branch. It merges cleanly with main.\n\n- The tangent loop now uses the selected-chain wire path (#3180) and the native arc writer of #2978 (`round_profile::iso`, `PunchSetup20`). It has no quality object of its own (#2984).\n- The old writer file of this PR and its top-level test binary `agie_dxf.rs` are not used. The tests are in the `agie_native::tangent` module, the post lib module `agie::tangent_profile_tests` and the geometry `wire_round_profile` tests.\n- A Ra 0.35 request on the tangent punch is refused, as for the other arc punches.\n- The new goldens `ROUND20.ISO` and `THREEARC.ISO` were imported on the emulated control. The readings are in the PR body. The other goldens do not change.\n- Quick gate: 1,201 steps, 0 failed. Strict Clippy passed for post, geometry, app and ui.\n- The decision file is now `docs/decisions/2983-wire-tangent-dxf.md`.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
